        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ആൾക്കൂട്ടം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആൾക്കൂട്ടം — āḷkkūṭṭaṁ — \"a throng; a crowd of people\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അപകടം നടന്ന സ്ഥലത്ത് വലിയ ആൾക്കൂട്ടം ഉണ്ടായിരുന്നു. apakaṭaṁ naṭanna sthalattŭ valiya āḷkkūṭṭaṁ uṇṭāyirunnu. There was a big crowd where the accident happened."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആൾ, a person, + കൂട്ടം, a group."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആൾക്കൂട്ടം (āḷkkūṭṭaṁ) is a native Dravidian compound of ആൾ (āḷ), \"a person\", and കൂട്ടം, \"a gathering, a group\", from the root of കൂടുക, \"to come together\" (DEDR 1882)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
